<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/u1.rs. std only. Compact U(1) Wilson lattice gauge theory (the program's counter-model; 4D Coulomb phase above beta ~ 1): angles theta per link (Torus::link_index), S = beta sum_p (1 - cos theta_p). Staple sum A = sum_j e^{i alpha_j} = k e^{i phi} so the local weight is exp(beta k cos(theta + phi)); heat bath theta = VonMises(beta k) - phi (Best-Fisher 1979 sampler, uniform for kappa < 1e-8); over-relaxation theta -> -2 phi - theta; angles wrapped to (-pi, pi]. Same checkerboard classes, Philox streams (seed, sweep, link, replica) and thread-count independence as wilson.rs. Observables: plaquette (mean cos theta_p), plaquette_angle; gauge_transform. torus_plaquette_u1_2d(beta, V): exact 2D torus value from Z = sum_n I_n(beta)^V. Independent tests in tests/u1.rs: von Mises marginal E cos = I_1/I_0; 2D Monte Carlo against the exact torus value; gauge invariance; identical links for 1 and 6 threads.
